# Intelligent Posture-Controlled Wheelchair

An assistive robotic wheelchair system that enables users to control movement using head or upper-body posture.  
The project aims to support individuals with mobility impairments by providing an intuitive and hands-free control system.

---

## Overview
This system detects body posture using sensors or computer vision and converts the detected signals into directional commands for wheelchair movement.

The goal of this project is to demonstrate how intelligent systems and assistive robotics can improve accessibility and independence for people with disabilities.

---

## Features
- Posture detection using sensors or computer vision
- Directional wheelchair control
- Assistive mobility support
- Real-time response to user movements

---

## Technologies Used
- Python
- OpenCV
- Arduino
- Sensor modules
- Embedded systems

---

## System Architecture
1. Sensors detect head or body posture
2. Data is processed using Python/OpenCV
3. Commands are generated for wheelchair movement
4. Arduino controls the motors based on commands

---

## Applications
- Assistive mobility for people with disabilities
- Rehabilitation technology
- Human–machine interaction research

